<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

Lane test-door (road M1): the commit broker gains a `test` door. A walled lead names test files; the broker runs them with node &#45;-test or the file's own package vitest inside a bwrap namespace (PID, IPC and network unshared, new session, clean env), binding only the worktree (its `.git` read-only from a held fd), scratch, the active Node version and system dirs. Every worktree path walks held O_NOFOLLOW segments; no parse error echoes file bytes; a named LIVENESS silence bound ends a hung run through killGroup; zero-test runs refuse; tallies stay advisory, never a receipt. The launcher P1-3 flake is cured by causal order (the stub prints before its token event). Canon: seat-harness #/the-broker names the door.

Reads: Luna, a blind Opus read and a fresh re-read, each cured. Suites: test-door 20/20, commit-relay 40/40 (the access witness among them), launch-codex 94/94 under load in a PID namespace.

